# MCSP Kernel Driver Builder Report 0.55

Status: Constructive report-boundary experiment
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parents:
- DETERMINE-CONDITION kernel lineage through 0.16
- DRIVER-BUILDER-INTERFACE-0.52.mcsp
- LINUX-KERNEL-OBJECT-PROJECTION-0.53.mcsp
- KBUILD-MODULE-INTEGRATION-0.54.mcsp

## Foundational notice: MCSP is a kernel

MCSP is not merely a language, assembler, driver generator, or Linux integration
layer. MCSP has its own kernel.

    MCSP KERNEL = DETERMINATE CONDITION

The MCSP kernel is the semantic and qualification center from which applicable
construction obligations are determined.

The Linux kernel is a distinct external operating-system kernel.

Therefore:

    MCSP kernel != Linux kernel

and coupling MCSP to Linux does not subordinate the MCSP kernel to Linux semantics.

Linux ABI, Kbuild, module metadata, return thunks, driver registration mechanisms,
and hardware APIs are downstream realization constraints when Linux is the chosen
projection.

## Objective

Produce a machine-representable driver-builder report from MCSP-kernel obligations
and carry that report toward a hardware/OS realization without allowing the target
kernel or driver builder to redefine the originating semantics.

## Report record

The bounded 0.55 record contains:

    schema
    semantic_relation
    width_or_extent
    source_role
    destination_role
    preservation
    replacement
    hardware_boundary
    access_mode
    transfer_mode
    interrupt_mode
    kernel_projection
    qualification
    unresolved_residue
    lineage

MODE is preferred to TYPE. STATE is not required.

## Propagation

    MCSP KERNEL
       DETERMINATE CONDITION
              |
              v
       semantic obligation
              |
              v
       hardware examination
              |
              v
       DRIVER-BUILDER REPORT
              |
              v
       driver builder
              |
              v
       MCSP Assembler / construction
              |
              v
       target kernel object/module
              |
              v
       Disassemble / Decompile / Verify
              |
              v
       REALIZE / SUSPEND / REJECT

## Authority direction

Semantic authority flows from the MCSP kernel obligation into the report.

Hardware observations constrain applicability and realization but do not rewrite
the originating semantic obligation.

The driver builder chooses implementation mechanisms within the report constraints.
The external kernel supplies its realization boundary.
Neither becomes the MCSP kernel.

## Bounded fixture

0.55 uses an x86-64/Linux projection with a bounded exclusive relation and a
driver-builder report declaring:
- width 64;
- source preserved;
- destination replaced;
- hardware boundary x86-64;
- access mode callable;
- transfer mode register;
- interrupt mode none;
- kernel projection Linux;
- qualified;
- no unresolved residue.

A compatible report may proceed to REALIZE.
Unknown hardware or unresolved compatibility shall SUSPEND.
Semantic mutation or incompatible construction shall REJECT.

## Boundary

This checkpoint does not load a driver, access hardware, register a Linux device,
or claim universal driver generation.

The MCSP kernel identity is architectural and semantic; 0.55 does not claim that
MCSP is an operating-system kernel equivalent to Linux.
